:23 (opposed to הִכְבִּיד ). Pilpel Perfect 3 masculine singular 1. shake קִלְקַל בַּחצִּים Ezek 21:26 (in divination). 2. (peculiarly) whet Eccl 10:10 (properly move quickly to and fro). Hithpalpel reflexive of 1. : Perfect 3 plural הִחְקַלְקָ֑לוּ Jer 4:24 hills shook themselves , shook.", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB7448')\">BDB7448</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H7043')\">H7043</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB7447')\">BDB7447</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB7449')\">BDB7449</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>קָלַל</bdbheb>]<sub>82</sub> <b>verb</b> <highlightword>be slight, swift, trifling</highlightword> (probably originally <highlight>be light</highlight>; Late Hebrew [<bdbheb>קָלַל</bdbheb>], <bdbheb>קַל</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>קִלֵּל</bdbheb>=Biblical Hebrew; Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>‡alâlu</highlight></transliteration> II. <highlight>depise, dishonour</highlight>; so Tel Amarna (apparently Canaanism); Arabic <placeholder4758/> <highlight>be small, scanty</highlight>; Sabean <bdbheb>קללם</bdbheb> <highlight>scanty</highlight> Hal 143.8f. (compare Fell<sup>ZMG liv (1900), 246</sup>); Ethiopic <placeholder4759/> <highlight>be light, Small, easy</highlight>; II. <highlight>despise</highlight>; Targum <bdbheb>קְלַל</bdbheb>, Syriac <placeholder4760/> = Biblical Hebrew; also (see <b>Pilpel</b>, etc.) Arabic <placeholder4761/> <highlight>shake</highlight>, <placeholder4762/>: <highlight>vibrate, whirl</highlight> (of sword), <placeholder4763/>: <highlight>see be shaken</highlight>; — <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Schw')\">Schw<sup>ZAW xi (1891), 170 ff.</sup></lookup> thinks <highlight>shake</highlight> original, see  <bdbheb><reflink>מַקֵּל</reflink></bdbheb>); — <div class=\"point\"><b>Qal</b> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> 2 masculine singular <bdbheb>קַלּוֺתָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Nah 1:14\" b=\"34\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(34,1,14)\">Nah 1:14</ref> 1 s